As a named developer I'm not really addressed by this but you will be
glad to hear that the upcoming release of UnNetHack will have a
working version of Vanilla's Windows GUI.

> they are neglecting a large portion of their potential audience. C'mon 
> gentlemen, it's not 1982 anymore, we can use tiles at the very least now. 

It depends on the quality of the included tiles version and frankly
the ones I know from Vanilla (x11, mswin, qt, gnome) don't really work
well IMO.

But I've also problems with Crawls excellent GUI version. The graphics
are just too detailed and sometimes hard to distinguish. If you've
never played the ASCII this might work you but I prefer something a
bit more distinguishable. It's a pity as the user interface is really
cool.

I'd really like something like the Abigaba tiles for Crawl:
http://bilious.alt.org/~paxed/nethack/nhsshot/?dump=0&tileset=abigaba

